1. The basic idea of RNNs is to provide short-term memory to the neurons.Neurons are connected to themselves through time.This self-connection allows one to remeber
the information that the neuron previously holds.Therefore,this connection helps pass the values a neuron holds to itself in the future to relate and analyze the information.

2. The feed-forward network should not be used to predict the succeeding words of a sentence,as the output in this model is independent of the previous outputs.In case
of RNN,output at a timestamp depends on the output's previous timestamps.Thus, ANNs designed to predict patterns in sequential data is known as RNNs.

3. The main limitation of RNN is long-term dependencies.When the timestamp is too long,the propagation of information from all the previous timestamps is challenging.
Further,this leads to issues like vanishing gradients and exploding gradients.

4. If a network has n hidden layers,n derivatives are multiplied together during gradient descent.So, when derivates are very small , an exponential decrease of the 
gradient value occurs as we traverse through model until it vanishes.This scenario is termed as the vanishing gradient problem.When the derivates are very large,an 
exponential increase of the gradient value occurs as we traverse through the model until the gradient value explodes.This scenario is termed as exploding gradient 
problem.

5.LSTM(Long Short Term Memory) is a type of RNN architecture designed to overcome the limitations of traditional RNNs in capturing and retaining information from long
sequences.

6.LSTM uses cell state and gates inside a cell.The cell state acts as a transport highway that passes the relevant information as it traverses down the neural network.
The cell state can be considered as the network's memory.It is primarily designed to carry the required information.It controls the effect of short-term memory.Gates
will learn the relevant information during the training phase and forget the unnecessary information.

7.The sigmoid function is used to keep or forget the information.

8.The forget gate decides which information to forget or which information to remember or pass to the next stage.The input gate decides the amount of useful information 
in the current input or information that needs to be added from the current step.Input gate and forget gate are used to calculate the current cell state.Finally,the 
output gate calculates the current hidden state.
